# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Allowlist policy: ignore everything, then re-include source and small results.
# Deliberate — the working folder is 1.7 GB, and with a blocklist one forgotten
# pattern in `git add -A` pushes hundreds of megabytes.
#
# New file type?      add a `!` line below.
# One specific file?  git add -f <path>
# What's hidden?      git status --ignored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*

# Descend into directories (without this, nothing below the root is reachable).
!*/

# --- source ----------------------------------------------------------------
!*.py
!*.ipynb
!*.smk
!*.sh

# --- config and docs -------------------------------------------------------
!*.md
!*.tex
!*.yaml
!*.yml
!*.toml
!*.cfg
!*.txt
!.gitignore
!.env.example

# --- slide decks (the framing a reader needs before the code) --------------
!*.pptx

# --- small result tables (inspectable without a full rerun) ----------------
!results/matcher/plant_matcher_output.xlsx
!results/plant_lookup_complete_with_coords.csv
!results/comparison_lookup_vs_matcher.csv
!results/comparison_matcher_conf_ge_0p5.csv
!figures/paper/claim_check.csv
!data/samples/*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excluded wholesale — re-ignored after the allowlist, so no `!` rule above can
# pull anything out of them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# PyPSA-Eur workflow intermediates and solved networks (1.2 GB + 124 MB).
# One .nc here exceeds GitHub's 100 MB hard limit.
resources/
results/de-nodal-2013/
results/de-nodal-2025-hourly/
results/test-elec/

# Third-party clone, has its own git history
pypsa-eur/

# Collaborator's repository, cloned for comparison — do not vendor it
reference_repo/

# Shadow-price exports (130 MB of CSV, no code)
Constraints_and_Shadow_Prices_v2/

# Siting sweep artefacts: 50 generated configs + 50 result CSVs per run
siting/out/

# Generated bitmaps — regenerate with maps/render_to_png.py and the notebooks
figures/**/*.png
figures/**/*.pdf

# Generated interactive maps — regenerate with maps/*.py
results/maps/

# Raw and joined data — see data/README.md for provenance
data/*.csv
data/*.parquet
data/*.xlsx
data/grid_data/

# --- python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.env
.venv/
venv/
